      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-11-28_WidnesExaminer_art0019" n="art0019">
        <head>CREWE.</head>
        <p>CREWE.</p>
        <p>The CHAIRMAN said it was now his pleasant dutyto introduce the Earl of Crewe to the meeting. (Cheer.) They welcomed him for three reasons. First they wel- comed him for his own sake—(hear, hear)—because he was taking off his coat in regard to the fiscal fight, and because he had filled responsible positions in the Government and had served his King and country loyally and well. (Applause.) They also welcomed him because he had a wife-laagther)—and might he give expression to the hope which had received some encouragement from the Earl that evening that his good lady would consider whether she would c nine to Warrington to open the Liberal Bizaar ? (Loud cheers, and a voice," Bring your father-in-law down." Laugh- ter and applause.) They also welcomed the earl, be- cause he was connected closely with one of the greatest statesmen of England—Lord Rosebery—(applause)— who was their last Liberal premier, and had spoken with decision and weight upon that fiscal question be- cause of the great love and desire he had to see the Empire consolidated and strengthened. It was because of that Imperial instinct—his desire to see the Empire strengthened—that he had given all his weight against proposals which , he thought would impair it. (Applause.) THE EARL'S SPEECH.</p>
        <p>SOME OF Mit CHAMBEFtLAIN?S STATEMENTS</p>
        <p>ANALYSED. "POLTTICALLY CRIMINAL.I!</p>
        <p>The EARL OF CREWE, who had a flattering reception, said he had much pleasure in seconding the resolution which had been moved by Mr. Crosfleld, and he hoped</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1903-11-28_WidnesExaminer_art0020" n="art0020">
        <head>LUNG DISEASES.</head>
        <p>LUNG DISEASES.</p>
        <p>The gev. %V. DACRE, 5, College Villa Road, S Hampstead. London, writes, June 17th :—" I have a high opinion of VE:so's LIGHTNING COUGH CURE. I have used it with much benefit to myself and have recommended it to others." VENo's LIGHTNING COUGH Cflur: is the purest and most efficient remedy procurable for coughs, cold,, bronchitis, asthma, catarrh, and children's coughs. Price Md., is. 14d., and 2s. 9d., at chemists and drug ores.</p>
