        <p>MUNICIPAL, ELECTION, 30TH NOVEMBER TO THE ELECTORS OF BEWSEY WARD LADIES AND GENTLEMEN. I have been unanimously adopted by the Liberal Ward Committee as the Candidate for the vacancy in the Council caused by the election of William Pier- point, Esq , as an Alderman of the Borough. If I have the honour to be elected on Monday next as your Representative I shall do my very utmost to merit your confidence. As I am not interested in any Firm or Company trading with the Corporation. I cannot be accused of having any "axe to grind " in asking you to vote for me. I am, however, greatly in favour of the inquiry being carried through without any further delay.and so clear the town of the unplea•antness that has existed during the past two years. There can be no real efficiensy in the work of the Council until the Inquiry has been finally disposed of. Any good scheme that comes before the Council which I think will benefit the Ward as regaids Street Improvement, better Lighting of the Streets. Cheaper has, Recreation Grounds for children,Trarn- ways, &amp;h.. shall have my warmest:support,but I shall always study efficiency with economy. Having lived in Your midsl all my life I am well acquainted with the requirements of your Ward and I trust, Ladies and Gentlemen, you will give me your support on Monlay next and elect me as your representative. I remain, Ladles and Gentlemen, Yours very sincerely. OW EN TOOLB. 64 Bewsej street, November 24th, 19)3.</p>
